  "description": "The inventory layout, read twice: rules 1-3 and 5-9 of the target schema's x-layout. Read 1, current resolved through its link: a writer's temporary name (.core-rtr-02.yaml.tmp) is ignored, as is a hidden name whose stem fails id's pattern; a file whose id differs from its stem is refused; a telnet file that does not validate is skipped and the rest loaded; a discovered_by that is not its source directory is refused; two sources holding one id load neither, and the alert names the id and both sources. Read 2, current missing: the index stays as it is and an alert is raised — it never empties. The reader never takes inventory/.lock, and a staging directory is never read. The rule is executable in tsbc (_inventory.inventory_read); this case is its record. `alerts` is the reader's report of what it refused; the core writes each as a log line (x-layout identity-and-refusals, missing-current).",
